  "body": "## Status: research note (scoped mechanism + complete cost recurrence; no new kappa)\r\n\r\nTrack **recursive-interfaces** (50-59), assignment seed **53** (OS CSPRNG). One\r\nexplicit way to eliminate boundary/restoration work with a complete cost\r\nrecurrence, a sufficient correctness condition (with the exact defect criterion\r\nbehind it), and a sharp cost boundary. Contributor:\r\n**Navinor (Aaron Wang)**, with help from opencode. Apache-2.0.\r\n\r\n### What is learned\r\n\r\nA recursion node that restores its borrowed dirty workspace after **every** child\r\npays `r` restoration passes. This note prices one operator-level rewrite: let the\r\nworkspace drift across the batch and replace the `r` restorations by the **one**\r\ncomposed restoration `(G_r...G_1)^{-1}` at the node exit. Two independent\r\nquestions decide it, both decidable exactly:\r\n\r\n- **Correctness (vanishing defect; read-free is sufficient, not necessary).**\r\n  The single deferred restoration returns the same observables (final data and\r\n  final workspace) exactly when the summed defect vanishes,\r\n  `sum_i B_i (G_{i-1}...G_1 - I) = 0`. Read-free batches make every term vanish\r\n  separately and are sufficient, but they are **not necessary**: nonzero readers\r\n  can cancel (exact counterexamples:\r\n  https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1199,\r\n  https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1203,\r\n  https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1205). The certificate's\r\n  reader example shows only that one reader child *can* break deferral; a second\r\n  case replays the exact nonzero-reader cancellation (5 restorations -> 1).\r\n- **Cost (composable family; density is not application cost).** The rewrite\r\n  removes passes only when the restoration operators stay cheap under\r\n  composition: unit phases -> one phase pass, permutations -> one routing pass\r\n  (`r -> 1`). The recurrence now charges composition explicitly under a succinct\r\n  descriptor hypothesis (fixed-size parameter tuples; `r * c_desc` with\r\n  `c_desc = O(1)`) and records `Theta(r * N)` to compose full length-`N`\r\n  descriptor tables outside it; the `N = 8` tests establish the tested\r\n  instances, not an unpriced general recurrence. A **heterogeneous** mix\r\n  (phase + Walsh + permutation) composes to\r\n  a dense product that *retains its cheap factorization*: applying the factors\r\n  sequentially costs the eager sum (`16` = `16` multiplications at `N = 8`,\r\n  verified against the exact dense product). Deferred application costs *more*\r\n  only when no cheap factorization is retained and the dense product must be\r\n  applied directly (`64` vs `16` multiplications at `N = 8` \u2014 a statement about\r\n  direct dense application). Structure, not the count alone, decides.\r\n\r\n### Reproduce\r\n\r\nStandard library only, Python 3.10+ (verified on 3.12 and 3.13), from the repo root:\r\n\r\n```sh\r\npython3 -I -O -B research/restoration-coalescing/verify.py\r\n```\r\n\r\nExpected first line:\r\n\r\n```\r\nPASS_RESTORATION_COALESCING phase=3->1(x3) perm=3->1 hetero_dense=True reader_diverges=True reader_cancels_5to1=True hetero_mults=eager16|factorized16|dense64\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe checker recomputes the certificate and compares every field with\r\n`research/restoration-coalescing/CERTIFICATE.json`, failing on drift. It builds\r\nevery operator explicitly at `N = 8` over exact Gaussian rationals (no floating\r\npoint, no random tolerance, no imported supplier verifier), derives each composed\r\nrestoration from the exact dense product, and self-checks any cheap structured\r\napplication against that product on the standard basis before trusting its cost.\r\n\r\n### Base commit and pins\r\n\r\n- Base: `ce7ad1b6ab09452c3478723a2e96ed5ff212dc08` (current `origin/main`).\r\n- Branch: `research/agent-13-recursive-seed53` (isolated research\r\n  package under `research/restoration-coalescing/`; no generator, `upstream/`, or\r\n  selected-construction file touched).\r\n- Selected result at base unchanged: `kappa = 836330098538459/500000000000000000`\r\n  ([PR 1094](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1094) on [PR 1087](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1087)).\r\n- Exact source/dependency pins and file digests: `research/restoration-coalescing/SOURCE-PINS.json`.\r\n\r\n### Relationship to concurrent work\r\n\r\nThis is a second, independent treatment of the restoration question with a\r\nmeaningfully different method (exact operator algebra and structure detection,\r\nstandalone sub-second, versus assembly-level pricing on frozen payloads). It does\r\n**not** claim priority on \"restoration deferral\" and does not reproduce others'\r\nnumbers.\r\n\r\n- [CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds#1012](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1012)\r\n  (thakrarsagar, same track) prices restoration deferral of U8 helper rank/frame\r\n  climbs at the hosted T37 assembly level and finds it mass-neutral. Different\r\n  layer and cost unit (rank mass vs. phase/routing passes); complementary, not a\r\n  contradiction.\r\n- [CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds#974](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/974)\r\n  (avirazza, same track) prices the same boundary classes with zero parent cost.\r\n\r\nWhere those notes give the assembly-level ceiling effect, this note gives the\r\noperator-level preconditions (vanishing summed defect + composable family) for a\r\ngenuine\r\n`r -> 1` pass reduction at all. Both are needed before deferral is placed in a\r\nreal supplier call.\r\n\r\n### Scope and inherited assumptions\r\n\r\nA restoration-elimination mechanism, its recurrence, and its exact applicability\r\nboundary. **Not** a construction, not a new kappa, not an all-size physical\r\ncompiler, precision contract, common tape, analytic transfer, owner schedule, or\r\nthe integer-multiplication theorem. Finite checks are exact algebraic identities\r\nand exact cost counts; they do not certify a whole E8 word or the selected\r\n`kappa`. Neither the selected frontier nor `upstream/` changes. Inherited\r\nall-size/compiler, hosting, precision/tape and analytic assumptions remain with\r\ntheir existing constructions. No independent human or proof-assistant review is\r\nclaimed. Relevant check run: the package's own verifier (full `make verify` and\r\nthe selected cold replay are untouched by this isolated package and were not run).\r\n\r\n",
